nodecode-hireko is a rewrite of HireKoAI's HireKoAI/HirekoAiPluginPublicRepo:

  https://github.com/HireKoAI/HirekoAiPluginPublicRepo
  commit 4af68d73ac89e67f8bc5f4a68d1079f1dc2c8294
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Hireko (LICENSE)

The rewritten plugin is its `.hermes-plugin` folder at that commit: a Node
stdio MCP server with no dependencies that signs a recruiter in to Hireko's
AWS Cognito user pool and proxies tool calls to Hireko's hosted MCP facade
over JSON-RPC. Its wire is carried over unchanged: the tenant's own
configuration page at recruiter-<tenant>[.beta].hireko.ai names the Cognito
app client and the pool's region, with the plugin's hard-coded client id and
us-east-1 as the fallback; InitiateAuth with USER_PASSWORD_AUTH, the email
and the password as AuthParameters and the X-Amz-Target header; one
`tools/call` per tool with the same arguments the plugin builds (the title,
a slugged external_job_group_id, both dates in epoch milliseconds, the
AllFunnels funnel, the recruiter's email or a default), the bearer token
plus the AuthorizationTenant, AuthorizationRegion and x-tenant headers; the
poll of get_interview_link until a jobId or an interview_link appears, the
candidate link built on interview-test[.<stage>].hireko.ai with the same
settings query; the session saved as one JSON file per tenant, 0600; the
answer shape (structuredContent, else content[0].text, else the error
text). LICENSE is the repository's LICENSE, unchanged.

The cell's section replaces the plugin manifest's environment variables
(tenant, stage, HIREKO_USERNAME, HIREKO_PASSWORD, the credential store),
and the session file lives under the Nodecode home.

What was left out, and why: the browser device login and its loopback
listener on a fixed port with an eight-byte state nonce, because Nodecode's
sign-in is a command and a password in the environment, so /hireko login
signs in through the same Cognito call headlessly; the stdio JSON-RPC
transport, tools/list and initialize, which the cell contract replaces; the
`login` tool the plugin handled but never advertised, since hireko_login is
advertised here; and Node itself, replaced by the image's own NLK:HTTP.
